{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>Behold, in heaven עד\"י</b> — in gematria חנוך, and שהד\"י in gematria מטטרון. The Holy One, blessed be He, took one of those from before the generation of the flood and one from after the generation of the flood, namely חנוך and פנחס, and concealed them to heaven, that they may testify concerning Him. And He chose חנוך, who was of the seventh generation, for the Holy One, blessed be He, desires seventhness. So too משה, who was seventh to the patriarchs, concerning him is written: 'and משה went up unto Elohim.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "The word לשמים ('to heaven') appears in the lemma phrase הנה בשמים but not in the cited verse Genesis 4:18; the lemma phrase seems drawn from a different context. The acronym עד\"י is left unresolved; the gematria equation הנה בשמים עד\"י = חנוך is reproduced as written. The verb והעלם read as 'and He concealed them' (possibly והעלים)."}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:15:43.157719845Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}